<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">28 June in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 28 June, from 1098 to 1919.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/crusader-states" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/crusader-states.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1098 CE <span class="tih-ago">928 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Crusaders break out of Antioch and rout Kerbogha</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Besieged in the city they had just taken, and inspired by the supposed discovery of the Holy <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lance">Lance</a>, the crusaders defeated the army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kerbogha">Kerbogha</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mosul">Mosul</a>. The road to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> lay open.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lance">Lance</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mosul">Mosul</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1519 CE <span class="tih-ago">507 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Charles of Spain is elected Holy Roman Emperor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-elector">electors</a> chose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles I of Spain</a> over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-i">Francis I</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. As Charles V he ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/low-countries">Low Countries</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> and much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperor</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/low-countries">Low Countries</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-i">Francis I</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1712 CE <span class="tih-ago">314 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Jean-Jacques Rousseau is born in Geneva</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jean-jacques-rousseau">Rousseau</a>'s The Social Contract and Émile shaped political thought and education, and his Confessions helped create modern autobiography. His ideas inspired French revolutionaries.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1914 CE <span class="tih-ago">112 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Archduke Franz Ferdinand is assassinated in Sarajevo</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gavrilo-princip">Gavrilo Princip</a> shot the heir to the Austro-Hungarian throne and his wife Sophie. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austria-Hungary</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-ultimatum-to-serbia">ultimatum to Serbia</a> set off the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/july-crisis">July Crisis</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/austro-hungarian-empire">Austro-Hungarian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gavrilo-princip">Gavrilo Princip</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/july-crisis">July Crisis</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1919 CE <span class="tih-ago">107 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Treaty of Versailles is signed</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> signed the peace in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hall-of-mirrors">Hall of Mirrors</a>, five years to the day after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sarajevo">Sarajevo</a>. It accepted territorial losses, disarmament and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-reparations">reparations</a>, which fuelled lasting resentment.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-versailles">Treaty of Versailles</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hall-of-mirrors">Hall of Mirrors</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sarajevo">Sarajevo</a></div></div></li></ol>
